          "text": "filename: docs/choir-summary.md\n# Choir Rehearsal Summary\n\n## Key Points  \nMarta led the warm-up and focused on breathing techniques for ten minutes, helping the group establish better control during singing. Owen arrived late due to a delayed bus, but still contributed by offering to print fresh copies of the score before Friday. Priya identified that the altos are rushing the second verse of the folk song \"Down by the River\" and suggested slowing the tempo to improve rhythm. The group successfully clapped the rhythm together to reinforce timing. Marta proposed marking breath points in everyone's sheet music to support consistent phrasing. The tenors continue to struggle with the high note near the end of the piece. The spring concert has been scheduled for the second Saturday of April. Tea and biscuits were provided by the hall committee, and everyone was reminded to bring a pencil and a water bottle.  \n\n## Next Steps  \nPriya will book the hall for two additional rehearsals in March to provide more practice time. Owen will print fresh copies of the score before Friday to ensure everyone has an updated version. Marta will implement the breath point markings in the sheet music for all singers. The group will continue to work on the high note for the tenors during upcoming sessions. All members should arrive at seven thirty sharp for the next rehearsal. The team will review the rhythm and phrasing during the next session to address the altos' rushing issue. A follow-up meeting will be scheduled to discuss progress on the spring concert preparations.",
